  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1237 PM CST Wed Nov 11 2026\n\nAfter a pristine fall Friday, we're looking at an active shift in \nour weather for the weekend, potentially recurring mid-late next \nweek. Breezy south winds return Saturday when a lead shortwave ahead \nof our next weather maker passes just south of the Panhandles, \nleaving a tighter pressure gradient over the region (sustained 15-20 \nmph gusting to 35 mph). These winds will advect better moisture \nnorthward to the Panhandles, with weak forcing from the shortwave\npotentially producing some light showers early Saturday morning- \nafternoon. The far more promising chance for rain should arrive \nwith the main low pressure system models show approaching from our\nnorthwest late Saturday into Sunday. This is when moisture and \nlift will be maximized across the region, before the system clears\nout Sunday night. Rain chances keep climbing for Saturday night \ninto Sunday, now greater than 70% across the eastern Panhandles, \nwith 40-70% probabilities for measurable rain further west. \n\nAny rain earlier Saturday would likely be on the lighter side, as \nlimited forcing and PWATs of 0.5-0.8\" are good but not great \n(especially with little to no CAPE). As we go into Sunday, moderate \nto heavier rain showers are expected across the east where PWATs \ncould be closer to 1\", leading to 40-70% chances for rainfall to \nexceed 0.5\". The way things are trending, most of the CWA would \nreceive only a tenth or two of an inch, with some locations in the \nwest staying even less than that. Looking at run to run ensemble \nupper level and QPF trends shows that this system has been gradually \nshifting further south, so we'll see if this leads to any \nsignificant changes to forecast expectations moving forward. \n\nTemperatures this weekend into next week are continuing to come in \nas below average (highs in 50s & lows in 30s), thanks to fairly \npersistent cloud cover over the area. Global models are holding onto \nthe notion that after a brief period of ridging early next week, \nadditional strong weather systems could approach the region. If this \npans out, breezy winds along with additional rain chances would be \nexpected. \n\nHarrel",
